    "ns-en-1995-1-1_2004+a2_2014+na_2024_en_001.pdf": {
        "document_text": "\n The document titled NS-EN 1995-1-1:2004+A2:2014+NA:2024 is the Norwegian version of Eurocode 5, which provides the design rules for timber structures, specifically general rules and rules for buildings. It consolidates previous standards and amendments, including updates to mechanical resistance, durability, deformation, fasteners, and joint design.\n\nThis standard outlines both general principles and specific calculations for timber construction, referencing structural actions (per EN 1990 to EN 1999), material behavior, and design parameters. It incorporates nationally determined parameters (NDPs) for use in Norway and emphasizes the need to align design practices with the Technical Regulations to the Planning and Building Act (pbl).\n\nKey variables and parameters mentioned in the document include:\n\nufin,ucreep,uinst\nu\nfin\n\t\u200b\n\n,u\ncreep\n\t\u200b\n\n,u\ninst\n\t\u200b\n\n \u2013 components of deformation.\n\nEmean,fin,Gmean,fin,Kser,fin\nE\nmean,fin\n\t\u200b\n\n,G\nmean,fin\n\t\u200b\n\n,K\nser,fin\n\t\u200b\n\n \u2013 final mean values of modulus of elasticity, shear modulus, and slip modulus.\n\n\u03c4d,Vd,fv,d,kcr\n\u03c4\nd\n\t\u200b\n\n,V\nd\n\t\u200b\n\n,f\nv,d\n\t\u200b\n\n,k\ncr\n\t\u200b\n\n \u2013 design shear stress, shear force, design shear strength, and crack factor.\n\nkdef,kmod,kc,90\nk\ndef\n\t\u200b\n\n,k\nmod\n\t\u200b\n\n,k\nc,90\n\t\u200b\n\n \u2013 deformation factor, modification factor for duration and service class, compression factor perpendicular to grain.\n\nFEd,MEd,FA,Ed,MA,Ed\nF\nEd\n\t\u200b\n\n,M\nEd\n\t\u200b\n\n,F\nA,Ed\n\t\u200b\n\n,M\nA,Ed\n\t\u200b\n\n \u2013 design forces and moments.\n\n\u03b1,\u03c1k,d,d1,dh\n\u03b1,\u03c1\nk\n\t\u200b\n\n,d,d\n1\n\t\u200b\n\n,d\nh\n\t\u200b\n\n \u2013 angle to grain, characteristic density, diameters of fasteners and screw heads.\n\na1,a2,a3,t,a4,c\na\n1\n\t\u200b\n\n,a\n2\n\t\u200b\n\n,a\n3\n\t\u200b\n\n,t,a\n4\n\t\u200b\n\n,c \u2013 minimum spacing and distances for connections.\n\nfax,k,Fax,\u03b1,Rk,nef\nf\nax,k\n\t\u200b\n\n,F\nax,\u03b1,Rk\n\t\u200b\n\n,n\nef\n\t\u200b\n\n \u2013 axial withdrawal strength and capacities, effective number of fasteners.\n\nThese variables are essential in evaluating load-bearing capacity, connection strength, and long-term performance of timber structures.\n",
        "document_embedding_b64encode": ""
    }
